class Solution {
    public List<String> findItinerary(List<List<String>> tickets) {
        List<String> itinerary = new ArrayList<>();
        Map<String, PriorityQueue<String>> adjMap = new HashMap<>();
        for(List<String> ticket : tickets){
            adjMap.computeIfAbsent(ticket.get(0), k -> new PriorityQueue<>());
            adjMap.get(ticket.get(0)).offer(ticket.get(1));
        }
        dfs(adjMap, itinerary, "JFK");
        Collections.reverse(itinerary);
        return itinerary;
    }
    private void dfs(Map<String, PriorityQueue<String>> adjMap, List<String> itinerary, String source){
        while(adjMap.containsKey(source) && ! adjMap.get(source).isEmpty()){
            dfs(adjMap, itinerary, adjMap.get(source).poll());
        }
        itinerary.add(source);
    }
}

Time : O(E log E)  :
For every edge, pq will sort neighboring edges O(E log E)
dfs -> poll takes O(log E) and this will heppend for every edge
O(E log E)
Space : O(V + E)
